# =============================================================================
# CivicResolve Mobile Environment Configuration Template (.env.example)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env in apps/mobile/ for local development.
#
# ARCHITECTURAL CLASSIFICATION & SECURITY RULES:
#
# 1. PUBLIC / CLIENT CONFIG
#    - SUPABASE_URL: Shared canonical Supabase endpoint.
#    - SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Publishable client JWT key.
#    * Safe for client-side storage because all authorization is enforced
#      server-side via PostgreSQL Row Level Security (RLS) policies.
#
# 2. CLIENT-EXPOSED CREDENTIAL WARNING (NON-PRODUCTION SECRET)
#    - GEMINI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY:
#      ⚠️ WARNING: When used directly in Flutter, this API key is embedded into
#      the client app bundle and can be extracted via APK decompilation/network inspection.
#      It is a CLIENT-EXPOSED credential suitable for development/testing only.
#      PRODUCTION HARDENING REQUIREMENT: Route all multimodal image classification
#      requests through a server-side proxy/Edge Function where the private key
#      remains strictly on the server.
#
# 3. SERVER-ONLY SECRETS (NEVER PLACE IN MOBILE / NEVER COMMIT)
#    - SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: STRICTLY FORBIDDEN IN MOBILE
#    - DATABASE_PASSWORD: STRICTLY FORBIDDEN IN MOBILE
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. PUBLIC / CLIENT CONFIG ---
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key-here

# --- 2. CLIENT-EXPOSED CREDENTIAL (DEV/PROTOTYPE ONLY) ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here
